  "description": "Follow-up spike from TASK-7.29 (decision: Q-4 a). Open-raise lines scale toward raw PFR and calling lines toward raw VPIP, which ignores position. For an ordinary 22/18 player at 100 hands the 6-max BTN open goes 34.54% to 18%, BB call-raise 41.48% to 22% and SB limp 44.65% to 22%. Reusing the TASK-7.29 ratio rule for calling lines would push loose players to 100% (BB call-raise at 60/45). Lay out options with measured numbers (e.g. ratio with a cap, ratio for open-raise only, keep) and record the user's decision. Evidence: doit/TASK-7.29/spec.md \u00a73 and the Q-4 options.",
